<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (Crop disease outbreaks, such as Northern Leaf Blight \(NLB\), threaten food security and economic stability for farming communities across Sub-Saharan Africa. Caused by a fast-spreading fungus, NLB can devastate entire maize harvests if not identified early. To address this, Engineers Without Borders at Cornell developed an open-source, non-commercial system that combines aerial and ground-based robotics with machine learning to detect early signs of disease in the field. For more information on this project check out: ewb-dig-ag.org Our team is now building a two-step YOLO and CNN model, with plans to deploy it on AWS SageMaker and host a public demo.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2 600 0 R 4]
>>
endobj
