<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Finger Lakes ReUse, a local secondhand reuse organization, struggles to process donations as quickly as they come in. The EWB Software Subteam is building a mobile marketplace where donors can list items and locals can arrange pickup, designed to be simple for users of all ages and abilities. Built with React Native, Expo, Node.js, Express, Supabase, and Stripe, with designs created in Figma, the app and database are now functional. The team is now connecting the front end to the back end so that customer requests can be connected to available stock, and adding notifications to make the user experience more convenient, before handing the app off to Finger Lakes ReUse. Our Software Subteam has also delivered a mobile app for Cornell Wardrobe that lets students rent professional clothing from their phones, and a carbon offsetting app for the Tompkins Climate Fund.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
